@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
rectangle "Untrusted transport / local injector" as Wire
rectangle "Authorized producers (compromise still possible)" {
 component Radar
 component Camera
 component ADAS
}
rectangle "Shared test-only keys / clock / retained-state abstraction" as Shared
rectangle "Authentication boundary (Python SiL adapters)" {
 component "Sensor ingress verifier" as Sensors
 component "Primary command verifier" as Primary
 component "Backup command verifier" as Backup
 component "Per-subscriber status verifiers" as Status
}
rectangle "Trusted local FFI / native ECU boundary" {
 component "C++ ADAS + safety supervisor" as Supervisor
 component "C++ Brake ECU + original E2E checks" as Brake
 component "C++ Body ECU" as Body
}
Wire --> Sensors
Wire --> Primary
Wire --> Backup
Wire --> Status
Radar --> Wire : authenticated acquisition data
Camera --> Wire : authenticated acquisition data
ADAS --> Wire : authenticated request / state
Shared --> Sensors
Shared --> Primary
Shared --> Backup
Shared --> Status
Sensors --> Supervisor : verified, then semantic gates
Primary --> Brake : verified 8-byte request
Backup --> Brake : verified 8-byte request
Status --> Body
Status --> Supervisor
Brake --> Wire : authenticated brake status
component "Single physical actuator / friction-limited plant" as Plant
Brake --> Plant
Plant --> Supervisor : trusted previous-step achieved deceleration
note bottom of Shared
Backup transport shares security dependencies and physical actuation.
MAC authenticates permitted producer; it cannot prove benign intent.
end note
@enduml
